cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TB-BTR data, annotations, or analysis code, please cite this record together with the original studies listed in Supplementary Table S1."
title: "TB-BTR: Tuberculosis Blood Transcriptome Resource"
type: dataset
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-27
abstract: >-
  TB-BTR is a curated resource of human blood transcriptome studies for
  tuberculosis research. Publicly deposited microarray and RNA-seq studies are
  assembled into a single catalogue with harmonised clinical phenotypes,
  documented treatment-interval provenance, participant linkage where the source
  permits, and derived expression and immune-cell profiles. The deposit contains
  the resource inventories, supplementary tables, field definitions, and the
  inputs and code needed to reproduce one comparative analysis of inferred
  immune-cell composition between active tuberculosis and latent infection.
authors:
  - family-names: Yuan
    given-names: Shaoxun
repository-code: "https://github.com/shaoxunyuan/TB-BTR"
url: "http://tbbtr.njucm-bioinfo.cn:9191/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - tuberculosis
  - transcriptomics
  - blood transcriptome
  - gene expression
  - immune-cell deconvolution
  - meta-analysis
  - curated database
  - reproducible research
